  "status": "Refused",
  "actual_commencement_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The submitted documents fail to demonstrate that the proposed use (Class B8) would be suitable and successfully integrate with its residential surroundings. Given the nature of Class B8, it would result in further unrestricted comings and goings to the unit to a level that is to the detriment of continued enjoyment of nearby residential dwellinghouses. This conflicts with the overall aspirations and priorities of the Council, whereby development (including changes of use) should be beneficial to the local community which it relates to. The principle of the change of use to B8 in this location is unacceptable, is fundamentally incompatible with its wider residential setting and is contrary to Policies 45 and 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Without evidence to the contrary, by virtue of its siting the development would be located within the root protection area of a number of mature street trees, which provide a positive contribution in terms of visual amenity and biodiversity in the area. The proposed replacement building is considered to cause harm to the setting of the trees and further harm to biodiversity cannot be ruled out. This is contrary to the objectives of Policy 80 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which looks to retain and protect trees.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
